First, I remember that blocking websites usually involves some form of filtering or restrictions. Maybe I can use a script that goes through each page and blocks access when certain keywords are found. I've heard of using regular expressions for pattern matching, so that might be useful here.

I think I should start by setting up the HTML structure. I need a basic HTML page that loads a script. The script will handle the blocking functionality. I'll include a loading bar and a message that changes based on the keywords found.

Next, I need to include a library for keywords or domains to block. Maybe I can create an array of URLs that I want to block. For each URL in the array, I'll check if it's present in the page's content. If it is, I'll trigger the blocking message.

I also want to add a way for the user to add more URLs to the block list. Perhaps a button that appends new URLs to the existing array. This way, the user can customize which sites are blocked.

The script should check the page content each time the page loads. Using JavaScript's eval function with document.body.innerHTML should allow me to execute the blocking logic. I'll write a function called blockAccess that runs whenever the DOM content changes.

I should also handle cases where the same URL is blocked multiple times. Maybe using a Set to track blocked URLs and prevent redundant checks. That way, if the same URL is blocked again, it won't trigger the message multiple times.

Testing is important. I'll make sure that the script works by visiting a blocked site and seeing if the message appears. Also, I'll check if adding new URLs to the block list works without errors.

I'm a bit concerned about security. Using this script on someone else's website could be against their terms of service. I should mention that this is a basic example and not suitable for production environments.

Finally, I'll outline some considerations like using a proper Content Security Policy, user education, and maybe a more secure blocking method like DNS filtering instead of blocking entire websites. This way, the user knows that this script is a starting point and they should implement more robust security measures.

Putting it all together, I'll structure the HTML with the necessary elements, include the script, and make sure it's clear how to customize the blocked URLs. I'll also provide some notes on better practices and security considerations.
